Round d1_r8 complete. Both deliverables are in place: `impl/d1_twiddle.c` (three changes, all node-verified by interleaved A/B against a true impl_7 reference) and a new "Round d1_r8" section appended to `strategies/d1_twiddle.md`. The headline: d1_batchlane's split-form register chains ported to 32/64/128, which flipped my two widest board losses — 64 B=1 chained 0.114→0.080 µs (−30%) and 128 B=1 chained 0.257→0.155 µs (−40%) on the scoring node, plus 32 B=1 chained 0.065→0.058 at donor parity. Also shipped: the driver-unit (≥20 ms) probe samples from race r7/prime r8 with a warm-recalibration fix of my own (the cold sizing calls silently shrank samples to 5 ms), and pow2 r7's NT threshold at 16 MB (steadies the 1024 B=512 median at 1.73). All graded gates pass, output bitwise repeatable, fallback builds (`-DD1TW_EXACTMAP`, `-DD1TW_SPLITCH=0`) verified.

Technique ended on: split-complex natural-row register chains (d1_batchlane's design fed by my exact v4 row-lane tables) + driver-unit placement probe; best wallaby: 0.028 µs/xf at 64 B=1 m=1 and 0.028 µs/xf batched (B=512), chains 0.048/0.062/0.117 µs at 32/64/128 B=1; rel L2 = 1.1–3.4e-16 (chain gates worst 1.17e-11 vs 1e-10).
